# --- build output ---------------------------------------------------------
# `dist/` holds the released binary and `dist_<ver>/` the candidate for the
# version being built; neither belongs in git.  A 37 MB one-file EXE would make
# every clone heavy, and because git keeps every blob forever, each future
# version would add another 37 MB to the history.  Releases are attached to a
# GitHub Release instead -- see the README.
dist/
dist_*/
build/
build_*/

# --- python ---------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.env

# --- tooling --------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor/agent scratch space: memory logs and per-session state, not sources.
.workbuddy/
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- internal recon -------------------------------------------------------
# Reconnaissance reports quote one specific mod's organisation, unit counts
# and naming quirks.  They are development notes for this editor, not
# documentation for whoever installs it, so they stay local.  The manual,
# `doc/NDFBIN编辑器使用说明.md`, *is* shipped -- the pattern stays deliberately
# narrow.
doc/*勘查报告.md

# --- third-party material --------------------------------------------------
# A decompiled copy of someone else's moddingSuite, its installer and tutorial
# documents, and the IL dumps taken beside them.  Useful while working out the
# format; none of it is ours to redistribute.
moddingSuite_reverse(OLD)/

# --- build products that are not the EXE -----------------------------------
# The packaged manual is generated from doc/*.md and doc/ui截图-*.png, both of
# which are already in the tree -- keeping a copy here would be 5 MB of
# duplicate that goes stale.  It belongs on a GitHub Release.
doc/WarnoNdfbinEditor说明文档/
doc/*.zip

# --- strays ----------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.bak

